    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Can You Change the Date of a Boat Trip in Madeira After Booking?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>19 December 2026</span><span>6 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Yes, as long as you ask more than 24 hours before departure. A direct Chifbay booking can be cancelled free of charge until then, so you can move to another free date, and if the skipper calls the trip off because of the sea, you choose a new date or a refund.</p>

      <h2>How do you move a direct booking to another day?</h2><p>Look at the calendar on chifbay.com first, find a date that is still open, then message us on WhatsApp with the name on the booking, the trip, and the day you would like instead. Do it as soon as your plans shift, not the evening before.</p><p>The rule underneath it is short. Up to 24 hours before departure, cancelling a direct booking costs nothing. That means you are never stuck with a date that no longer works: at worst you cancel, and book the new day yourself. In practice, a message is quicker for everyone and keeps the conversation in one place.</p><p>Two things to check before you pick the new day:</p><ul><li><strong>The departure time.</strong> Day Trip departures are at ten in the morning or two in the afternoon. The evening trip is timed from the sunset itself, 75 minutes ahead of it, so on a new date its start can sit half an hour or more away from your old booking, especially across the clock change at the end of March or October.</li><li><strong>The rest of your week.</strong> A levada walk the morning after a late Sunset Trip, or a flight on the afternoon of a Day Trip, is easy to overlook when you are only thinking about the boat.</li></ul><h2>What if it is less than 24 hours before the trip?</h2><p>Then the free window has closed. Chifbay's terms say that a refund may not be possible after that point, because nobody else could be offered your slot, and a date that close is very hard to fill again.</p><p>Ask anyway. Message us on WhatsApp with what has happened and what you would like. Just do not count on a yes, and do not leave it until the morning of the trip. A no-show, where nobody turns up and nobody writes, is treated under the same terms as a trip taken.</p><h2>What happens when the sea changes the plan?</h2><p>This is the date change that happens most, and it is not your decision to make. When the skipper judges the water too rough for a small boat, the outing is off, and the choice that follows is yours: rebook for a calmer day or have the payment returned.</p><p>A grey sky is not the trigger. Swell and wind are. Madeira's south coast is usually the sheltered side of the island, but a big swell from the west or south west, or strong gusts, can make the coast past Cabo Girão uncomfortable or unsafe for a small boat. Portugal's weather institute, IPMA, issues coloured sea warnings for the island, and the Funchal harbour authority publishes its own notices on rough days. Our guide to <a href="/posts/what-happens-to-a-boat-trip-in-madeira-in-bad-weather">a boat trip in bad weather</a> explains how the call is made.</p><p>The simplest protection is timing. Book the trip early in your holiday. On a week's stay, if the sea says no on day two, you still have five days to move it. If it says no on your last morning, you have none.</p><h2>Is it different if you booked on a platform?</h2><p>Yes. If you booked through GetYourGuide, Viator or Click&amp;Boat, the platform holds your booking and your payment, so a change or a cancellation starts there, under the policy shown on that listing. The boat, the skippers and the route are the same whichever site you used, but the paperwork is not.</p><ul><li><strong>GetYourGuide.</strong> Plenty of experiences there can be cancelled for free until a day before they begin, yet the terms printed on the listing are the ones that bind. Manage the change from your booking in the app or on the website.</li><li><strong>Viator.</strong> Each listing shows its own cancellation terms. If you used the option to reserve now and pay later, your card is charged on a date shown in your booking, which matters if you cancel close to it.</li><li><strong>Click&amp;Boat.</strong> The cancellation policy is shown on the listing. Its help pages explain that service fees and the platform's commission are kept even when the rental itself is refunded, so read that line before you pay.</li></ul><p>Whatever the platform, you can also send us a WhatsApp message so we know what is happening. We cannot move money that a platform holds, but we can tell you whether the new date is free. For the wider choice between booking routes, read <a href="/posts/book-madeira-boat-trip-direct-or-getyourguide">booking direct or on GetYourGuide</a>.</p><h2>What applies in each situation?</h2><p>The table sets the common cases side by side. The terms on your own booking always win.</p><table><thead><tr><th>When you ask</th><th>Booked on chifbay.com</th><th>Booked on a platform</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>More than 24 hours before departure</td><td>Free to cancel, so you can move to any open date</td><td>Use the platform's own change or cancel option, under its listing's policy</td></tr><tr><td>Less than 24 hours before</td><td>Ask on WhatsApp, but a refund may not be possible</td><td>The platform's policy applies, contact it first</td></tr><tr><td>The skipper cancels for the sea</td><td>New date or full refund, your choice</td><td>New date or full refund, with any refund paid back through the platform</td></tr><tr><td>Nobody turns up</td><td>Treated as a trip taken, no refund</td><td>The platform's no-show terms apply</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Can you change the time, the trip or the group instead?</h2><p>Often, yes, and these smaller changes are usually easier than a new date. Ask on WhatsApp and say exactly what you want.</p><h3>A different time on the same day</h3><p>Switching from the 10:00 to the 14:00 Day Trip depends only on whether the afternoon slot is free. The same is true the other way round.</p><h3>A longer or shorter trip, or the other trip</h3><p>Moving between the 2h30 and 3h Day Trip, or from the Day Trip to the Sunset Trip, changes the price, because each option has its own price per boat: 500 or 600 EUR for the Day Trip, 400 or 500 EUR for the Sunset Trip. The <a href="/experiences">page with both trips</a> shows what each includes.</p><h3>One more person, or one fewer</h3><p>The price is for the whole boat, so going from three guests to four does not change it, as long as you stay within the limit of five. Tell us anyway, so the skipper knows who is coming. Our page on <a href="/posts/can-you-add-a-guest-to-a-private-boat-trip-booking">adding a guest after booking</a> goes into detail.</p><h2>When is it better not to move it at all?</h2><p>When the new date is the last whole day of your holiday, or the morning of your flight. A trip pushed to the end of a holiday has no spare day behind it if the sea turns. If your first date still works, even imperfectly, keeping it is often the smarter choice.</p><p>The <a href="/practical">practical information page</a> keeps the cancellation rule next to the meeting point and the departure times, which is handy to have open while you decide.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is it free to change a Chifbay booking?</h3><p>Yes, if you do it more than 24 hours before departure. Cancelling is free until then, so you can move to any date that is still open.</p><h3>Who decides whether a trip moves because of the weather?</h3><p>The skipper. If the sea is not safe, the trip is off and you choose a new date or your money back.</p><h3>I booked on GetYourGuide. Can Chifbay change my date?</h3><p>Start the change on GetYourGuide, which holds your booking and payment. You can also message us on WhatsApp to check the new date is free.</p><h3>Can I switch from the Day Trip to the Sunset Trip?</h3><p>Usually, if the evening slot is free. Ask on WhatsApp. The price follows the trip and length you end up on.</p>

      <blockquote>Move it early, move it once, and keep a spare day in the holiday for the sea.</blockquote>
    </article>
    <p class="pref-src" data-pref-source><span>Enjoying our Madeira guides?</span> <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=chifbay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M23.5 12.3c0-.8-.1-1.6-.2-2.3H12v4.5h6.5a5.6 5.6 0 0 1-2.4 3.6v3h3.9c2.2-2.1 3.5-5.1 3.5-8.8z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M12 24c3.2 0 6-1.1 7.9-2.9l-3.9-3c-1.1.7-2.4 1.2-4 1.2-3.1 0-5.7-2.1-6.6-4.9h-4v3.1A12 12 0 0 0 12 24z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M5.4 14.4a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 0-4.7V6.6h-4a12 12 0 0 0 0 10.8l4-3z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M12 4.8c1.7 0 3.3.6 4.6 1.8l3.4-3.4A12 12 0 0 0 1.4 6.6l4 3.1C6.3 6.9 8.9 4.8 12 4.8z"/></svg>Add Chifbay as a preferred source on Google</a></p>

